 RESONANCE PARAMETERS                                           &&6640 1451
 Evaluation, 2001 by S.Y. Oh (KAERI)                            &&6640 1451
                                                                  6640 1451
 * Resolved resonance parameters from [Mu84] except parameters of 6640 1451
   a bound level with which the thermal capture cross section     6640 1451
   of 600 b and bound coherent scattering length of 10.3 fm       6640 1451
   [Mu84] were reproduced.                                        6640 1451
                                                                  6640 1451
  Calculated thermal cross sections & resonance integrals:      &&6640 1451
      ---------------------------------------------             &&6640 1451
      Reaction       Cross section    Res. integral             &&6640 1451
                        (barn)           (barn)                 &&6640 1451
      Total           6.17691E+02           -                   &&6640 1451
      Elastic         1.74834E+01           -                   &&6640 1451
      Capture         6.00208E+02      1.07373E+03              &&6640 1451
      ---------------------------------------------             &&6640 1451
                                                                  6640 1451
 * Average parameters for the unresolved region [0.996-25.812 keV]6640 1451
                                                                  6640 1451
     Wave  Strength Function  Level Spacing(eV)  Gamma Width(meV) 6640 1451
     ----  -----------------  -----------------  ---------------- 6640 1451
      s       1.79 E-4           1.73              106.8          6640 1451
      p       1.41 E-4           0.95               84.7          6640 1451
      d       1.79 E-4           0.74              106.8          6640 1451
                                                                  6640 1451
   The level spacing varys with energy according to the Bethe's   6640 1451
   formula with relevant parameters from [Mu98].                  6640 1451
   S0 from the Porter-Thomas analysis of resolved resonances.     6640 1451
   D0, S1 and Gg1 were adjusted to reproduce Voss+ avg. capture   6640 1451
   cross sections[Vo99] in the URR. S2 and Gg2 were assumed.      6640 1451
